Third-party notice: Grain LFSR code from hadeshash
==================================================

poseidon_bls12_381_reference.sage in this directory contains a port of the Grain LFSR constant
generator from the repository

  https://extgit.isec.tugraz.at/krypto/hadeshash
  (commit 208b5a164c6a252b137997694d90931b2bb851c5, 2023-05-02, file
  code/generate_parameters_grain.sage)

The Grain LFSR functions (the section marked "Grain LFSR (verbatim port)") follow that file
closely. They are adapted to fixed parameters (GF(p), x^alpha, t = 3, RF = 8, RP = 57) instead of
command-line arguments. The Poseidon permutation and the test-vector driver in the same file are
ZeroJ's own, written from the Poseidon paper.

The original code is by the authors of the Poseidon hash function: L. Grassi, D. Khovratovich,
C. Rechberger, A. Roy and M. Schofnegger, "Poseidon: A New Hash Function for Zero-Knowledge Proof
Systems" (USENIX Security 2021). Credit for it belongs to them and to Graz University of
Technology.

  File                                  SHA-256
  poseidon_bls12_381_reference.sage     270f62f23514dd2f8afb6630385ddac9ea1a5e524fa0473011866b28a37e33b0

sage-reference-output.txt is the output of running that script, not copied material.


